  "name": "clarify",
  "description": "Pins down what a user actually wants before work starts on an ambiguous or underspecified request — surfaces the competing interpretations and asks the clarifying question that removes the most uncertainty. Use when a request has multiple valid readings, critical details or constraints are missing, or it contradicts itself, and the gap would change the approach. Not for: well-specified tasks (renames, typo fixes, version bumps, running tests or commands, edits naming an explicit file and change), details readable from the codebase, or research and planning workflows that own their own scoping.",
